{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Go, descend, for your people has corrupted.</b> It should have said נשחת (has been corrupted), but the sense of שחת (corrupted) is upward and downward — in thought and in deed. And the meaning of שחתה is the tearing down of a structure, and this is what the Rabbis, of blessed memory, call קצץ בנטיעות (he cut down the plantings). And there is no doubt that this was like the deed of the first father who sinned in the Tree of Knowledge in deed and in thought, and מעשה אבות עשו בנים (the deeds of the fathers are done by the sons). To this the Rabbis, of blessed memory, alluded when they said of him that he offered a bull, for he wished to gain atonement through that with which he sinned; and understand this." "<b>And by way of the Midrash.</b> ״לך רד כי שחת עמך״ — the creatures have already caused Me to descend and to see their corruption, as it is said (Genesis 11:5): ״וירד ה׳ לראות״ and so forth; you too, descend from your greatness — it is enough for the servant to be like his master."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The phrase קצץ בנטיעות is a rabbinic idiom (Leviticus Rabbah) meaning one who undermines or destroys foundational structures; left in Hebrew as he cites it as a term."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:06:11.442436866Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}